<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.huffmanwrites.essay-watch</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/prh/Developer/huffmanwrites/scripts/essay-watch-runner.sh</string>
  </array>
  <!-- Keeps two published essays current without being asked. "The Year the
       Floor Moved" opens on a Mississippi margin a call will replace and states
       a Senate balance two calls will change; "The Tally" rests on two day-count
       series that can stop. Philip, 2026-11-04: "Keep those essays current
       without any prompting from me."

       One fire a day at 09:30 CT, fifteen minutes after nord-stream-watch and
       well clear of the 06:00 SITREP and its 07:00 watchdog. Both jobs read
       network feeds; neither publishes on a healthy day, so the two slots are
       cheap and ordering them apart keeps two pushes from racing.

       No RunAtLoad: a login is not a reason to re-check a race that has not been
       called. There is no end date here because the question has none — the
       essays carry claims that expire on their own schedule, and the runner
       exits 0 the moment nothing is stale. -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key>
    <integer>9</integer>
    <key>Minute</key>
    <integer>30</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Developer/huffmanwrites</string>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Library/Logs/essay-watch.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Library/Logs/essay-watch.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
